\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {XVI}{\ignorespaces The uncalibrated cosine proxy (LongMemEval oracle; tail-AUC over buckets with $\leq 3$ contributors, $0.5 =$ no leakage). \textbf  {Retained for contrast only.} The tail it stratifies on is all but \emph  {empty} at $K \leq 128$ (${\leq }0.03\%$ of members, i.e.\ a handful of targets, too few to score), so the proxy has nothing to report at the recommended operating point, while the calibrated attack of \S  \ref {sec:lira} breaks that same release (Table~\ref {tab:frontier}). Reading privacy off this table alone is the error \S  \ref {sec:proxy-blind} documents. The ``above chance'' column is computed from the unrounded mean and std, so it will not reproduce exactly from the rounded cells printed here.}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
